feat(web): make the Gemini composer model switchable

The web channel had exactly one model because the model is not in the
request. StreamGenerate never carries a model parameter -- the model is
ACCOUNT STATE, owned by the composer mode button. A bridge that only POSTs
StreamGenerate therefore always serves whatever mode the account happened to
be left in, which is what "网页端没办法切换模型" actually was.

Four real models are now offered: gemini-web-flash-lite / -flash / -pro /
-argon. gemini-web stays the "follow the account" default and deliberately
sends no switch RPC.

The switch is batchexecute L5adhe: a sparse array whose ONLY meaningful index
is 99 (the 16-hex model id), with the length repeated as the third element.
f.sid is WIZ_global_data.FdrFJe and bl is cfb2h; swapping them still returns
200, so a status code proves nothing.

Three silent-failure traps are now covered by regression tests:

- Pill parsing only understood fullwidth quotes, so an English UI returned the
  whole aria-label, labelMatches never matched, and the switch RPC was re-sent
  on every request while appearing to succeed.
- labelMatches used plain substring containment, and "flash-lite" contains
  "flash" -- the bridge would believe it had switched to Flash while the
  account sat on Flash-Lite and never correct it.
- Thread keys were prompt-only. A conversationId belongs to the account that
  created it, so rotation handed pro1's id to pro2 and the upstream answered
  200 with an empty body, indistinguishable from a degraded account.

Also: gemini-3.5-flash-lite was listed as a web alias despite being a real agy
model id, which routed agy traffic onto the web channel.

How to tell the switch worked, since the obvious signals lie: the model name
sometimes echoed in the response is a UI string unrelated to the mode, and
answer length / latency / easy-question accuracy are identical across tiers.
The toolchain is the discriminator -- on identical prompts Argon makes 2.2x the
python calls and 2x the analysis-tool calls of Flash-Lite. Verify with
bridge/tools/probe-toolchain.mjs, not with length.

Tests: 158 pass (17 new in bridge/test/modes.test.mjs).
